; Workspace build environment (board #69). The default (dev) profile is unchanged — it
; keeps OCaml assertions ON, so `make test` and the whole dev loop exercise every [assert]
; and debug self-check. The `release` profile additionally compiles with `-noassert`,
; disabling assertion checks: this is the config an official, PROMOTABLE corpus measurement
; is built under (`dune build --profile release`; see tests/corpus + `make promote-baseline`),
; so per-file effort/timing is not inflated by assertion overhead. `corpus_classify --stamp`
; then reports `assertions=off`, which the fail-closed promote gate requires.

(env
 (release
  (flags
   (:standard -noassert)))
 ; o3 (board: OxCaml -O3 measurement toolchain). Same source, same -noassert as
 ; `release`, but built with OxCaml's flambda2 ocamlopt at -O3. This profile is
 ; ONLY meaningful when the OxCaml toolchain is first on PATH (its ocamlopt.opt
 ; understands -O3); the default/release profiles on the standard opam toolchain
 ; are byte-unchanged. Two link flags accommodate the nix-built OxCaml runtime on
 ; this el8 box: -ldl (el8 glibc 2.28 keeps dlopen/dlsym in a separate libdl that
 ; the runtime's link line omits) and a small C shim object supplying the C23
 ; __isoc23_strtol family that libasmrun.a references but el8 glibc predates. The
 ; shim path comes from $OXSMT_O3_SHIM so the branch carries no machine path.
 (o3
  (flags
   (:standard -noassert))
  (ocamlopt_flags
   (:standard -O3))
  (link_flags
   (:standard -cclib -ldl -cclib %{env:OXSMT_O3_SHIM=isoc23_shim.o}))))
